# errors with the structured diagnostic formats
#
# --error-format changes how an error is printed, not whether it is caught.
# An uncaught error in human format names the file, the line and the reason;
# json format is the same facts in a shape a tool can read; short format is
# one line. Caught errors print nothing at all in any format, because a caught
# error is a value and values do not print themselves.
#
# The expectations here are the legacy format's, which is the default. The
# other two are exercised by tests/diagnostics.sh, which asserts on their
# structure rather than pinning every byte.

# caught: nothing on stderr, nothing on stdout
try {
	throw Error("swallowed")
} catch e {
	print(e.message)
}

# uncaught: the message, then a trace, then exit code 70
throw Error("this one is not caught")